From: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 17:20:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: reduce AN7563 TX completion writes

The AN7563 transmit path overwrites every descriptor word before handing
the descriptor back to QDMA.  Its original completion path therefore
clears only the two message words after unmapping a completed fragment.

The unified path additionally clears the control, address, next-index and
third message words for every completion.  Avoid those redundant coherent
memory writes on AN7563 while retaining the defensive cleanup for the other
SoCs.

Signed-off-by: X-WRT <dev@x-wrt.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 17 +++++++++++------
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -2935,12 +2935,17 @@ static int airoha_qdma_tx_napi_poll
 		e->skb = NULL;
 		list_add_tail(&e->list, &q->tx_list);
 
-		WRITE_ONCE(desc->ctrl, 0);
-		WRITE_ONCE(desc->addr, 0);
-		WRITE_ONCE(desc->data, 0);
-		WRITE_ONCE(desc->msg0, 0);
-		WRITE_ONCE(desc->msg1, 0);
-		WRITE_ONCE(desc->msg2, 0);
+		if (airoha_is(eth, airoha_an7563)) {
+			WRITE_ONCE(desc->msg0, 0);
+			WRITE_ONCE(desc->msg1, 0);
+		} else {
+			WRITE_ONCE(desc->ctrl, 0);
+			WRITE_ONCE(desc->addr, 0);
+			WRITE_ONCE(desc->data, 0);
+			WRITE_ONCE(desc->msg0, 0);
+			WRITE_ONCE(desc->msg1, 0);
+			WRITE_ONCE(desc->msg2, 0);
+		}
 		q->queued--;
 
 		if (skb) {
-- 
2.51.0
